WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:04.370
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.706
-I've been trying to keep up
with everybody

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.641
during the pandemic. Like,
I've been trying to keep up

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.276
with my granddad, 'cause he's,

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.711
you know,
one of my favorite people.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.613
And he helped raise me
and everything.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.315
So sometimes I'll call. He lives
in an assisted living facility.

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.051
And so I'll call him, and one
of the things that happens --

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.654
These people are doing
an incredible job.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.523
But one of the things
that inevitably happens

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:28.460
is every time I call, they hand
the phone to the wrong old man.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.363
[ Laughter ]
Every single time.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.664
So then, through the phone,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.967
I have to guide an old man
to my granddad, right?

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:37.169
And the last few times,
they kept handing the phone

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.905
to the same wrong old man
named JB.

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:42.274
He's a lovely man,
but he's not my granddad.

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:43.309
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.211
And so they hand
the phone to JB.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.779
And I'm pretty sure
his name is JB

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:51.017
because he was born before
full names came out, alright?

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.119
This dude was born when there
were J's and there were B's,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.754
and then he put them together,
you know?

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.022
He is the most 98-year-old man

00:00:57.022 --> 00:00:59.626
I have ever come in contact with
in my life.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.795
So then they hand the phone
to JB, and I say, "Hello, JB,"

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:06.199
and then he says,
"How do you know who I am?"

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.101
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.403
And then I have to
explain to him,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:14.140
"Sir, I'm actually
your roommate's grandson, okay?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.108
So we've actually had
lots of conversations.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:17.243
I was just wondering

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.345
if you could hand the phone
to my granddad."

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.347
And then he's like, "I don't
think I know who that is."

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.582
And I'm like,
"Yes, sir, you do.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.251
He's your roommate.
He should be right there."

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.086
And he's like,
"I'm not sure about that."

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.921
And so then finally,
I have to ask him,

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:33.426
"Sir, is there an old Black man
wearing a conductor's hat

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.529
sitting on a bed
watching Westerns?"

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.299
And then JB goes,
"How do you know that?"

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.336
And then I have to spend 15
minutes explaining to this man

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.906
that I am not the government,
alright?

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.908
I don't even know
what JB did in his life

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.311
to think the po-po
would still be after him.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.245
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:55.381
It was insane.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.949
And so finally, I can hear him

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:59.119
trying to get
my granddad's attention.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.686
And through the receiver,
I can hear him

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.054
and hear my granddad be like,

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.356
"Can't you see
I'm watching something?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.458
Leave me alone. I'm busy."
Right?

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.227
So then JB goes "I don't think
he wants to talk."

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.563
So then I just talk to JB.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.764
And honestly, it's nice.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.434
It's like having two granddads
again, you know?

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.002
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.205
'Cause I don't know
if you're all as well-versed

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.507
with old Black men as I am.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.643
I don't know if they're
as intimately in your lives,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.346
but is it just me,

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:30.115
or when old Black men
are about to fight,

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:31.284
doesn't it sound like

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.487
they're about to tear
into a piece of pie?

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.822
They're just standing in front
of each other like, "Mm-hmm.

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.826
[ Chuckles ] Mm-hmm.
Alright. Okay.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.461
Mm-hmm-hmm.
You about to get it, alright?

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.664
You about to get beat,
alright? Alright?"

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.565
And then they give you
the recipe of the fight.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.668
Like, "I'm-a take these hands,
alright?

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.637
I'm-a put a little foot
in it, okay?

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.538
I'm-a add some cane to it."

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.707
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:58.177
I've been watching a lot of TV.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.347
And I've been watching
a lot of rom-coms especially.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.350
And I don't know
if this bothers anybody else,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.818
but does it trip you out

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:09.756
that everyone in a rom-com has
enough money to make it work?

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.257
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.759
You know what I mean? Every
rom-com scenario is the same.

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.194
It's like boy meets girl.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.630
Boy falls in love with girl.
Boy messes it up.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:22.334
Boy buys a last-minute, day-of
flight to Australia, one way,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.337
to get past the gate
and stop girl

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.039
from taking a life-changing
opportunity across the world.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.742
It's like, I don't have
last-minute flight money,

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.578
alright?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.814
Like, even if I managed
to get that ticket,

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.883
I now have to go with you
to Australia,

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.685
whether I win you back or not,
you know?

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.487
Just running -- running
onto the plane

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.923
like, "Sheila, look,
I'm so sorry, okay?

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.490
I'm sorry, alright?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.193
I was stupid. I was dumb.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.094
I cared more about my friends

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:51.530
than the things that were
important to me, which is you.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.898
You're the most
important thing to me.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.701
You make me better,
you make me whole,

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.503
and I just want you
to take me back, alright?

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.572
Will you?

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:02.175
No? Okay, well, move over,
'cause I'm window.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.509
Alright? I --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.811
I really thought
this would work,

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:08.981
but, you know, buckle up
for 16 hours of awkward."

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:10.516
Like, just once, I want to see,

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:13.653
like, a realistic rom-com,
you know?

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.256
I want to see a rom-com where
they can't afford to break up.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.426
You know? Like, boy meets girl,
boy falls in love with girl,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.928
boy messes it up,
boy wants to move out,

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:26.198
but in a fit of passion,
they signed a lease.

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:30.569
So looks like this is life for
the next six months, playboy.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.305
Guys, I'm Josh Johnson.
Thanks so much.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.472
You have a great night.
Appreciate it.

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:36.475
Thank you so much
for coming out.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:37.777
-Josh Johnson!

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:41.414
For more info, go to
joshjohnsoncomedy.com.

